chumer and  Pelosi did like the proverbial  two-dollar banjo to minimize further  damage to the very fabric of human  civilization and the political  conventional wisdom again rushes to  reassure itself that its cliches still  work that he's pivoting in some way that  he's suddenly a cross-party pragmatist  that he's an independent that he's a bla  bla bla bla bla nonsense he's right this  time we people just really effing hate  him may I remind you of the headlines of  the last six weeks after the Nazis and  the KKK rallied in Virginia Trump made a  boilerplate statement about blame on  many sides then come issued a generic  statement that somebody else wrote then  Trump repudiated that statement in a  news conference of uncontrolled rage in  which he shouted about how both sides  were equally guilty then Trump held a  rally at which he read back his first  statement but left out the part about  many sides Trump threatened North Korea  with fire and fury Trump threatened  South Korea economically Trump  threatened Venezuela Trump went back and  threatened North Korea again Trump  pardoned Joe Arpaio Trump said he  pardoned our paio during a hurricane  because the TV ratings would be higher  Trump tweeted during the first hurricane  plugging a book by another infamous now  former sheriff Trump men tweeted during  the hurricane about building a wall to  keep out people of the same heritage as  a huge percentage of the victims of the  hurricane Trump traveled to Texas twice  during that hurricane the first time he  saw neither a victim nor a storm Trump  demanded tax cuts for rich people to be  speeded up because of the second  hurricane Trump referred to the Coast  Guard during the second hurricane as a  quote brand that has quote improved  Trump was repudiated about civil rights  by his own secretary of state Trump was  repudiated about transgender rights by  his own Secretary of Defense Trump was  repudiated about anti-semitism  by his own chairman of the White House  Economic Council Trump was so mad at the  chairman of his White House Economic  Council that he reportedly refused to  make eye contact with him  Trump's former senior adviser said in a  TV interview that any senator or  congressman who voted to impeach Trump  would be endangering their own lives and  that there would be a civil war Trump  reneged on the promise of daca blamed  Congress and then made a vague promise  to the dreamers in a tweet Trump turned  out to reportedly have written a first  draft of a letter justifying the firing  of the FBI director for not clearing him  on Russia Trump turned out to have at  least weighed in and maybe just wrote  the untrue statement issued by his own  son about a meeting his son had with  middlemen his son believed were giving  him Russian government dirt on Hillary  Clinton that's all just in the last six  weeks one would think that even in the  warped minds of those who think all that  was good news there is one basic human  emotion enough already I am exhausted I  want to watch something else in my life  besides Trump the key thing about tragic  heroes from the plays of the ancient  Greeks through Shakespeare is that they  all have that moment of Revelation that  epiphany of Lord what have I done  the people effing hate me but from  Oedipus to Hamlet it has to come too  late to make any difference  and usually the tragic hero is still not  getting some of the message that the  universe is sending him thus if the  Trump quote presidency unquote is  classic tragedy then the quote that  Axios attributed to a trump advisor was  necessarily missing a couple of words it  isn't people really effing hate me it's  we the people really effing hate you  resist remove peace my new book of these  commentaries and other writings which I  really should have called people really  effing hate him is available for  pre-order and will be out October 17th I  know I know I just said even those who  like Trump are exhausted by him I am too  just buy the book and wait for him to go  and  read it a couple of months after that  Thanks

